## givn commands

```sh
givn new <id>                          # create a new change
givn instructions <artifact> --change <id>   # show what to produce
givn lint                              # static .feature check (no tests)
givn apply --change <id>              # show task progress
givn status                           # lifecycle state of all changes
givn check <artifact> --change <id>  # run artifact post hooks
givn archive --change <id>           # gate + merge + move to archive/
givn eject <artifact>:<facet>        # pull embedded default into project
givn skills sync                     # regenerate this file + skills
```

---

## opencode commands

If you are using opencode, the following slash commands are available:

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/givn-propose` | Start a new change — create it and write the proposal |
| `/givn-spec` | Write Gherkin `.feature` delta files |
| `/givn-design` | Write the technical design (HOW layer) |
| `/givn-tasks` | Write the scenario-by-scenario task list |
| `/givn-implement` | Execute the RED/GREEN/REFACTOR TDD loop |
| `/givn-review` | Complete the coverage review and sign off |
| `/givn-archive` | Run gate hooks, merge delta specs, archive the change |

Each command optionally accepts a change ID as an argument (e.g. `/givn-propose add-user-auth`).

